## What could NOT be run locally in this session

$ cd services/gateway && npm ci
npm error code E403
npm error 403 403 Forbidden - GET https://registry.npmjs.org/zod/-/zod-3.25.76.tgz
npm error 403 In most cases, you or one of your dependencies are requesting
npm error 403 a package version that is forbidden by your security policy
(this sandbox's outbound egress policy blocks npm registry access; per this
session's own proxy guidance, a 403 from the proxy is to be reported, not
retried or routed around)

Consequence: `npm run build`, `tsc --noEmit`, and the gateway jest suite
could not be executed in this local sandbox. This PR's own "Build Gate"
step (`cd services/gateway && npm ci && npm run build`, in this same
VALIDATOR-CHECK workflow, running on a GitHub-hosted runner with normal
registry access) is the actual, real verification for compilation —
see its own job output on this PR. The updated jest fixture
(`test/middleware/auth-supabase-jwt.test.ts`'s fake Supabase chain now
stubs `.abortSignal()`, required because the real `@supabase/supabase-js`
query builder's `.abortSignal()` is now called by production code) was
written to match this repo's existing per-table thenable mock pattern
exactly, but was not independently run against a real jest process by
this session.
